ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaoE/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaoE/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"subscribed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2023-04-01T09:06:34Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/comments/1493529645","html_url":"https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/94128#issuecomment-1493529645","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/pytorch/issues/94128","id":1493529645,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA-j9z85ZBXQt","user":{"login":"CaoE","id":23565213,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNTY1MjEz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23565213?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaoE","html_url":"https://github.com/CaoE","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaoE/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaoE/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaoE/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaoE/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaoE/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaoE/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaoE/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaoE/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CaoE/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-04-03T01:59:00Z","updated_at":"2023-04-03T01:59:00Z","body":"@ezyang The root cause of such segmentations is the stride overflow of empty tensor. Pytorch can not catches stride overflow (int64 overflow) for empty tensor, although there is already `safe_compute_numel` which catches overflows for the non-empty case. When it comes with Symint, a segmentation may occur since Symint may treat it as a reference. Should we add stride overflow like https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pu